 ### Object-space AImC
-An approach to avoid suppression of context behind the focus object by suppressing only those samples of the context object that are in front of the focus object [S4, unofficial]. The countersink geometry defines the region of different levels of sparseness, but the starting position of the ray is not changed [S4, unofficial]. During the ray traversal of final image synthesis, each sample location is evaluated whether it belongs to the countersink area or not [S4, unofficial]. Outside the countersink area, the context is represented using a more dense representation, and inside, a more sparse form is chosen [S4, unofficial]. Unlike image-space AImC where the level of sparseness is constant for all samples of one object along a particular ray, object-space AImC has a level of sparseness that is not constant for one object along a particular ray [S4, unofficial].
+An approach to avoid suppression of context behind the focus object by suppressing only those samples of the context object that are in front of the focus object [S5]. The countersink geometry defines the region of different levels of sparseness, but the starting position of the ray is not changed [S5]. During the ray traversal of final image synthesis, each sample location is evaluated whether it belongs to the countersink area or not [S5]. Outside the countersink area, the context is represented using a more dense representation, and inside, a more sparse form is chosen [S5]. Unlike image-space AImC where the level of sparseness is constant for all samples of one object along a particular ray, object-space AImC has a level of sparseness that is not constant for one object along a particular ray [S5].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Depends on the sparsity of the grid and the distribution of occupied space. In the worst case (fully occupied), it is $O(N \cdot M)$ where $N$ is the number of rays and $M$ is the maximum samples per ray [S1, unofficial]. In practice, it is significantly faster due to skipping empty space [G].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N \cdot M)$ for output buffers if pre-allocated, or $O(\text{total\_samples})$ if dynamically resized. The density bitfield size depends on the grid resolution and hierarchy [S1, S2, unofficial].
